3. Subsystem Inventory
3.1 Acquisition Layer
Live WebSocket — persistent connection to ngrok tunnel forwarding fs5000_serial.py output; auto-reconnect on drop
JSONL Replay — file-based realtime playback at 1× speed, full pipeline fidelity
JSONL Fast Process — entire recording ingested synchronously; all derived values, ledgers, and waveform history populated instantly
Gzip support — .jsonl.gz decompressed in-browser via DecompressionStream
3.2 Signal Conditioning Layer
DR stable-display gate — string-level comparison of toFixed(4) output with 300ms minimum inter-update interval; matches serial.py terminal behavior exactly
Rolling averages — 30-second, 60-second, and 1-hour sliding windows computed from drHistory[] on every reading
CPM rolling window — 60-second count-per-minute derived from raw CPS stream
Session dose accumulator — running integral of DR × Δt
Device dose passthrough — hardware-reported cumulative dose preserved separately
3.3 Event Analysis Layer
Floor/peak detector — identifies state transitions between LOW/ELEVATED, records {fVal, pVal, dtSec, peakHrEq} pairs
CPS sequence recorder — captures integer CPS arrays across events for pattern comparison
Recurrence engine — compares new CPS sequences against ledger using edit-distance / subsequence matching; maintains hit counts and timestamps per signature
Beat interference detector — scores periodic constructive/destructive interference in CPS history
Alarm exposure timer — tracks cumulative time spent above L1 (0.18), L2 (0.23), L3 (0.27) µSv/h thresholds, per-hour and total
Exceedance logger — timestamped records when any rolling window exceeds 0.300 µSv/h reference
3.4 Evidence Ledger Layer
CPS signature ledger — numbered, sortable by value or time, persists full CPS sequence per entry
Floor→peak pairs log — chronological record of every detected elevation event with rise time and peak-hour equivalent
Raw telemetry stream — unprocessed [timestamp] DR=x CPS=x DOSE=x log, scrolling, preserved in order
Recurrence ledger — per-signature recurrence count, last-seen time, sequence thumbnail
Exceedance log — sub-ledger of threshold breach events with per-window breakdown
3.5 Output Layer
Waveform oscilloscope — canvas-rendered DR history, floor/peak dashed markers, CPS bar underlay, Δt annotation, panorama zoom mode
Rolling threshold monitors — color-coded 30s/60s/1hr readouts, amber at 80% of reference, red above reference
FS-5000/RadPro reference panel — device constants, SECOND/MINUTE/HOUR/YEAR projections, rolling window display
L1/L2/L3 siren — threshold-gated audio alarm with per-level tone
Panorama mode — full-history zoom/pan oscilloscope with click-to-inspect
Replay system — realtime file playback with progress bar and filename display
Export log — full session data exportable as JSONL
